{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["The interpretation of <b>והארץ תעזב מהם</b> (\"and the land shall be forsaken of them\"): for even after the visitation it shall be forsaken of them. This is a hint that after the visitation of Cyrus it was forsaken of them, and the sabbatical years ran until after nineteen years from when the House was built and the city was sanctified with two thanksgiving offerings (Nehemiah 12:31), and the sanctity of the land returned, and they cut a covenant (Nehemiah 10:1), and they said (Nehemiah 10:32), \"ונטש את השנה השביעית ומשא כל יד\" (\"and we will forsake the seventh year and the debt of every hand\"). All these matters are alluded to in this section."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The verse quoted from Nehemiah 10:32 uses ונטש (\"we will forsake/leave\"), echoing the root עזב in the lemma; the phrase משא כל יד refers to debts of every hand, per the context of the Nehemiah covenant."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:01:06.648305016Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}